.TH SHADOWSERVER 1 "November 2026" "shadowserver pipeline" "User Commands"
.\" no hyphenation / left-aligned, so file names and URLs stay readable and copyable
.nr HY 0
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
shadowserver \- pull Shadowserver reports from e\-mail and load them into MongoDB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shadowserver run
.RB [ \-\-stage
.IR all | email | load ]
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-workers
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-q | \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-env\-file
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B shadowserver check
.br
.B shadowserver status
.br
.B shadowserver logs
.RB [ \-f ]
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B shadowserver schedule
.RI [ HH:MM
.RB | off | show ]
.br
.B shadowserver deploy
.RB [ \-\-schedule
.IR HH:MM ]
.RB [ \-\-unschedule ]
.RB [ \-\-remove\-container ]
.RB [ \-\-uninstall\-commands ]
.br
.B shadowserver
.RB [ help | man | version ]
.SH COMMANDS
.B shadowserver
works from any folder; it is a link in
.I /usr/local/bin
to
.I bin/shadowserver
in the project folder, installed by
.BR deploy .
The project scripts
.BR ./run.sh ,
.B ./check.sh
and
.B ./deploy.sh
can still be used directly and take the same options.
.TP
.BR run " [options]"
Run the pipeline (see OPTIONS). This is the default: options without a
command, e.g.
.BR "shadowserver \-\-days 8" ,
mean
.BR run .
.TP
.B check
Full setup check: MongoDB binaries, the mongod service and its memory limit,
/etc/mongod.conf, login, cache size, unique indexes, document structure, data
folders, unfinished loads and the IMAP login. Exit status 1 if anything failed.
.TP
.B status
Short overview: mongod service and memory, number of services and rows in the
database, report files on disk, whether a run is in progress, the summary of
the last run, and the schedule.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \-f "] [" \fIN\fR ]
Last
.I N
lines (default 40) of the newest log;
.B \-f
keeps following it (Ctrl\-C to stop).
.TP
.BR schedule " [" \fIHH:MM\fR | off | show ]
Run the pipeline automatically every day.
.B "schedule 06:30"
sets (or changes) the daily time,
.B "schedule off"
removes it, and
.B schedule
alone shows it. No sudo needed. See SCHEDULING.
.TP
.BR deploy " [options]"
Install or update everything (asks for sudo): MongoDB from the official
repository, /etc/mongod.conf, the systemd memory limit, the MongoDB user,
the Python environment, data folders, and this command with its manual and tab
completion. Safe to run again at any time.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-schedule " HH:MM"
Also set the daily run, same as
.BR "shadowserver schedule" " \fIHH:MM\fR."
.TP
.B \-\-unschedule
Remove the daily run, same as
.BR "shadowserver schedule off" .
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-container
Delete the old Docker MongoDB container and volume (only after its data was migrated).
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-commands
Remove the global command, man page and completion (project files stay).
.RE
.TP
.BR help ", " man ", " version
Short help, this manual, version and project folder.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shadowserver run
runs
.BR shadowserver_pipeline.py ,
which replaces the two original scripts
.I pull_emails_and_create_services.py
(no longer shipped) and
.I mongo_added_json.py
(kept for the equivalence tests).
A full run has three steps:
.TP
.B 1. E\-mail
Logs in to the IMAP mailbox (read\-only, messages stay unread), fetches the
messages of the last
.I N
days, saves new attachments to
.I attachments_backup/
and, for e\-mails without a new attachment, downloads the
.I https://dl.shadowserver.org/
links they contain.
.TP
.B 2. Unzip and sort
Extracts each new zip once. Report files named
.I YYYY\-MM\-DD\-<service>[\-<number>]\-<country>\-geo[_asNNNN].csv
go to
.IR sorting_backup/<service>/ ;
everything else goes to
.IR unzipped_backup/<zip\ name>/ .
Corrupt zips are deleted. Loose report CSVs in the attachment folder are moved
the same way.
.TP
.B 3. Load
Every CSV/JSON file in
.I sorting_backup/
that is not yet in MongoDB is loaded by parallel worker processes. Files
already in the database are skipped, so repeated runs only load new reports.
.PP
Only one run can be active at a time (a lock file); a second run exits
immediately. All output is also appended to
.IR logs/pipeline\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.log .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-stage " " all | email | load
Which steps to run.
.B all
(default) runs everything;
.B email
runs steps 1 and 2 only (no database);
.B load
runs step 3 only (no e\-mail), e.g. to rebuild the database from files on disk.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Pull e\-mails received in the last
.I N
days. Default:
.B EMAIL_DAYS
from
.IR .env ,
normally 1 (since yesterday, like the original script). Use a larger value to
catch up after a gap, e.g.
.BR "\-\-days 8" .
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel loader processes. Default:
.B WORKERS
from
.IR .env ,
normally 6. Each uses about 100\-200 MB of RAM; lower it if memory is tight.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Summary lines only. Used by the daily cron job.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also print attachments that were already saved, and debug information.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Verify the setup and exit: configuration, Python packages, data folders,
memory, MongoDB login, cache size, unique indexes, document structure,
unfinished loads and the IMAP login. Exit status 1 if any check fails.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " PATH"
Read settings from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR ./.env .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Short help.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Show this manual.
.SH OUTPUT
By default each action is printed on its own line:
.PP
.nf
.RS
[EMAIL 12/1200] <date> | <subject> | 1 new attachment(s)
    [ATTACHMENT] saved <file> (412.3 KB)
[LINK 3/53] downloaded <file> (88.1 KB)
[UNZIP 2/40] <zip> \-> 1 report CSV(s)
    [SORT] <file> \-> <service>        (OVERWRITE if it replaced a file)
[MOVE] <file> \-> <service>
[SCAN] <service>  9 file(s): 0 already in MongoDB, 9 to load
[LOAD 5/412] <service>/<file>: 1,200 rows inserted (0.1s)
.RE
.fi
.PP
Progress lines (every 100 e\-mails, every 10 seconds while loading) and a
summary for each step follow. Problems are logged as
.B WARNING
or
.BR ERROR ;
anything that failed is retried on the next run.
.SH SCHEDULING
.TP
.B shadowserver schedule 06:30
Run the full pipeline every day at 06:30 (24\-hour clock, the time shown by
.BR date
in WSL). Running it again with another time replaces the old time; there is
only ever one daily run.
.TP
.B shadowserver schedule
Show the time, the cron line and where the logs go.
.TP
.B shadowserver schedule off
Remove the daily run.
.PP
The daily run is a cron job of your own user (see
.BR "crontab \-l" ,
marked
.IR "# shadowserver\-pipeline" ).
It runs
.BR "run.sh \-\-quiet" :
e\-mail of the last
.B EMAIL_DAYS
days, unzip/sort, load into MongoDB. Output is appended to
.IR logs/pipeline\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.log ;
check it with
.B shadowserver logs
or
.BR "shadowserver status" .
If a manual run is still going at that time, the scheduled run skips itself.
.PP
.B Important on WSL:
cron only fires while WSL is running, and WSL shuts down by itself when no
terminal or app uses it. Keep a WSL terminal open at the scheduled time, or
start WSL before it. If a day is missed, catch up with
.BR "shadowserver run \-\-days" " \fIN\fR."
.SH DATABASE LAYOUT
Database
.B shadowserver
(setting
.BR MONGO_DB ),
the same as the original scripts:
.TP
.I <service>
One document per unique CSV row: the CSV columns plus
.BR filename ,
.BR category ,
.B line_hash
(SHA\-256 of the row), and, when the
.B timestamp
column parses as
.IR "YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM:SS" ,
.B logged_date
(string) and
.B extracted_date
(date). Unique index on
.RB ( filename ", " category ", " line_hash ).
Rows whose timestamp cannot be parsed are skipped, as before.
.TP
.I discovered_fields_<service>
One document
.RB { category ", " field_name }
per CSV column seen.
.TP
.I files_<service>
One document
.RB { filename ", " category ", " path }
per file in the service folder.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I .env
(see
.IR .env.example ).
Values are taken literally, so passwords may contain $, # or @.
.TP
.BR IMAP_SERVER ", " IMAP_USER ", " IMAP_PASSWORD ", " IMAP_FOLDER
Mailbox to read (folder default
.BR inbox ).
.TP
.B IMAP_VERIFY_TLS
.B true
(default) verifies the mail server's certificate;
.B false
skips it, only for a server with a self-signed certificate.
.TP
.B EMAIL_DAYS
Default for
.BR \-\-days .
.TP
.BR MONGO_HOST ", " MONGO_PORT ", " MONGO_USER ", " MONGO_PASSWORD ", " MONGO_AUTH_SOURCE ", " MONGO_DB
MongoDB connection (default 127.0.0.1:27017, auth source admin, database shadowserver).
.TP
.BR MONGO_SERIES ", " MONGO_CACHE_GB ", " MONGO_MEMORY_LIMIT
Used by
.BR deploy.sh :
MongoDB release installed (8.0), WiredTiger cache (1.5 GB), and the hard
memory cap of the mongod service (3g).
.TP
.B DATA_DIR
Folder holding attachments_backup/, unzipped_backup/ and sorting_backup/
(default: the project folder).
.TP
.BR WORKERS ", " INSERT_CHUNK ", " DOWNLOAD_THREADS ", " IMAP_FETCH_BATCH
Tuning: loader processes (6), rows per bulk insert (2000), parallel link
downloads (4), e\-mails per IMAP round trip (25).
.TP
.BR ZIP_MAX_UNPACKED_MB ", " ZIP_MAX_RATIO ", " ZIP_MAX_FILES ", " ZIP_KEEP_FREE_MB
Unpacking limits against zip bombs: unpacked size of one zip (2048 MB),
compression ratio of one file (200), files per zip (100), disk space kept
free (1024 MB). Real bytes are counted while unpacking; a zip that breaks a
limit is moved to quarantine/ with a .reason.txt and is not retried. Low disk
space is not the zip's fault: that zip is tried again next run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env
Settings and credentials (mode 600).
.TP
.IR attachments_backup/ ", " unzipped_backup/ ", " sorting_backup/
Downloaded attachments, extracted zip contents, and report CSVs by service.
.TP
.I logs/pipeline\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.log
Run logs.
.TP
.I .pipeline_state.sqlite
Files whose load was interrupted; they are completed on the next run.
.TP
.I backups/
Database exports made by
.BR deploy.sh .
.TP
.IR /etc/mongod.conf ", " /var/lib/mongodb ", " /var/log/mongodb/mongod.log
MongoDB configuration, data and log (service
.BR mongod ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A file failed to load, the e\-mail step failed, a check failed, or another run
was already in progress.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C (unfinished loads resume on the next run).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B shadowserver run
Normal daily run.
.TP
.B shadowserver run \-\-days 8
Catch up on the last 8 days of e\-mail.
.TP
.B shadowserver run \-\-stage load
Load the files already on disk, e.g. after reinstalling MongoDB.
.TP
.B shadowserver run \-\-stage email \-\-days 3 \-v
Download and sort only, showing everything.
.TP
.B shadowserver status
Is MongoDB up, how much data, how did the last run go.
.TP
.B shadowserver logs \-f
Watch a run that is in progress (e.g. the cron job).
.TP
.B shadowserver check
Verify the whole setup.
.TP
.B shadowserver schedule 06:30
Run automatically every day at 06:30.
.TP
.B shadowserver schedule off
Stop the daily run.
.TP
.B sudo systemctl status mongod
MongoDB service status.
.TP
.B mongosh \-u <MONGO_USER> \-\-authenticationDatabase admin shadowserver
Open the database in the MongoDB shell.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mongod (1),
.BR mongosh (1),
.BR mongodump (1),
.BR crontab (1),
.I README.md
in the project folder.
